---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL
const limitationsUrl = `${base}docs/reference/known-limitations/`

const stats = [
  { k: 'bundled engine', v: 'none' },
  { k: 'rendering', v: 'system webview' },
  { k: 'engine updates', v: 'patched by the os' },
  { k: 'unused features', v: 'zero cost' },
]
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>04 &middot; engineering</p>
    <h2 class="section-title" data-reveal>light, because there is<br /><em>nothing to carry</em>.</h2>
    <p class="section-lede" data-reveal>
      wis renders with the engine your os already ships: webkit on macos and
      linux, webview2 on windows. no bundled chromium means a tiny download,
      less memory, safari-class speed and battery on the mac, and an engine
      the os keeps patched.
      the shell is rust end to end.
    </p>
    <div class="stats">
      {
        stats.map((s, i) => (
          <div class="stat card-g" data-reveal style={`transition-delay:${i * 70}ms`}>
            <p class="k mono">{s.k}</p>
            <p class="v" data-decode>{s.v}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="honest" data-reveal>
      the same choice has costs: no widevine drm, no browser extensions.
      <a href={limitationsUrl}>they are listed plainly in the docs.</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 48px;
  }

  .stat {
    padding: 26px;
  }

  .k {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-3);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .v {
    font-size: 21px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--lila-300);
  }

  .honest {
    margin-top: 34px;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--text-2);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .honest a {
    color: var(--peri);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .stats {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .stats {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
